<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<!-- Deploy wwwroot contents to the app's root, not _content/SpawnDev.WebTorrent/ -->
		<!-- Required for service worker scope — SW must be at app root to intercept all requests -->
		<StaticWebAssetBasePath Condition="$(StaticWebAssetBasePath) == ''">/</StaticWebAssetBasePath>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<Version>3.1.3-rc.3</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>v3.1.3-rc.3: Dep-bump to SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3-rc.2 which exposes per-association SCTP burst tunables on SpawnDev.SIPSorcery 10.0.5-rc.2. Consumers that know their link is loopback / LAN can raise MaxBurst (default 4, tune 32) to recover throughput the RFC default caps at MAX_BURST*MTU/RTT. Unblocks SpawnDev.ILGPU.P2P's 10 MB tensor transfer test that was bottlenecked by the RFC default at ~186 KB/s despite Riker's rc.1 Reset-race fix. No SpawnDev.WebTorrent source changes. Also preserves the 3.1.3-rc.2 body: v3.1.3-rc.2: Multiple BEP 52 v2 + data-channel performance fixes. (1) Pure-v2 multi-file download now works past file 0: TorrentParser flattens all files' piece-layer hashes in file-tree walk order (not just FileRoots[0]), per-file offsets reflect the BEP 52 padded virtual stream, and per-piece length is computed from per-file tails so short pieces straddling file ends verify correctly. New test VerifyPieceHashTests.V2_PureMultiFile_AllPiecesVerify_PastFile0 exercises a 3-file pure-v2 create-parse-verify round-trip with partial last pieces. (2) Wire._message now issues one _push per logical Wire message instead of two (header + data). Each BEP 10 extension message previously became two separate SCTP user messages on the WebRTC data channel; SCTP paced each independently, which stacked on top of SCTP MAX_BURST / BURST_PERIOD rate limiting and bottlenecked SpawnDev.ILGPU.P2P multi-MB tensor transfers at ~100 KB/s end-to-end despite the underlying pipe sustaining 5.4 MB/s on single-send payloads. (3) Hardens Torrent.DisposeAsync against late-firing Rechoke timer callbacks by using Timer.DisposeAsync to drain in-flight work, plus a defensive null filter + try/catch inside the callback. Full NUnit regression 256/0/0 in 5s. v3.1.3-rc.1: SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3-rc.1 dep bump (SctpDataSender reset-race fix, 60x loopback throughput win).</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
		<DebugType>Embedded</DebugType>
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
		<Title>SpawnDev.WebTorrent</Title>
		<Authors>LostBeard</Authors>
		<Description>Pure C# BitTorrent/WebTorrent client. 15 BEPs, real WebRTC P2P (browser + desktop), DHT with mutable items (BEP 46 — AI agent communication), web seeds, media streaming with seeking via service worker, OPFS storage. Includes webtorrent-sw.js for COI headers + torrent streaming. No JavaScript dependencies. Runs on desktop (.NET + SIPSorcery) and browser (Blazor WASM + SpawnDev.BlazorJS). 444 unit tests.</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>BitTorrent;WebTorrent;P2P;Torrent;Blazor;WebAssembly;WebRTC;DHT;Streaming;MachineLearning;ModelDelivery;SIPSorcery</PackageTags>
		<NoPackageAnalysis>true</NoPackageAnalysis>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Demo.Shared" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\icon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS" Version="3.5.3" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.AsyncFileSystem" Version="1.2.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS.Cryptography" Version="3.2.0" />
		<!-- SpawnDev.RTC replaces direct SipSorcery dependency - provides cross-platform WebRTC
		     with proven browser-interop SipSorcery fork (SRTP profile fix) bundled inside.
		     PackageReference (not ProjectReference) so CI / GitHub Pages builds work from a
		     standalone SpawnDev.WebTorrent checkout - they don't have the sibling RTC repo.
		     1.1.1 is the minimum version: 1.1.0 declared a dep on public SIPSorcery 10.0.4-pre
		     which doesn't exist on nuget.org; 1.1.1 bundles the fork DLLs inline (ILGPU pattern). -->
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.RTC" Version="1.1.3-rc.2" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="windows" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="linux" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="macos" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
